{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Lee. I understand you came in because your dialysis fistula wasn’t working today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, at dialysis they said no blood was flowing. My right arm fistula—just stopped working. I didn’t feel any pain or anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. We checked with an ultrasound, and it shows the graft is completely clotted. That’s why the blood couldn’t flow through."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. Is that dangerous? I’ve had this fistula less than a year."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s serious because you need it for dialysis, but we can fix it. The interventional radiology team will do a procedure tomorrow to clear the clot and open up the blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be able to go home after?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see how it goes. You’ll likely stay one night, maybe two. You’ll get dialysis here while we fix the fistula."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. My wife is here—she can help translate if I don’t understand."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thank you. We’ll make sure you both understand everything. For now, you need to stay NPO—nothing to eat or drink—after midnight in case of the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Nothing to eat? Even water?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No food or drink, not even water, after midnight. It’s for your safety during the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my blood pressure and labs—they looked okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are stable. Potassium is a bit high at 5.3, but not dangerous right now. Your kidney numbers are expected for someone on dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve had high potassium before—caused heart issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2159-04-23 16:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw that in your history. We’ll be careful with your medications and make sure you get dialysis soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2159-04-24 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. The radiology team is ready to do the procedure. They’ll use a special machine to open the clot in your fistula."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2159-04-24 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2159-04-24 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’ll give you medicine to help you relax and numb the area. You might feel some pressure, but not sharp pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2159-04-24 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And they’ll fix the whole thing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2159-04-24 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’ll clear the clot and open up a narrowing in the vein. But they’re concerned it might narrow again, so you may need another procedure soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2159-04-24 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it might happen again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2159-04-24 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. They found a tight spot in the large vein near your chest. Even after opening it, it could close again. They’ll schedule a follow-up in the next two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2159-04-24 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back from the procedure. They successfully cleared the clot and opened the narrowed vein using balloons."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2159-04-24 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I felt some pressure, but okay. Is it fixed now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2159-04-24 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The fistula is working again—there’s good blood flow and a strong thrill. But there’s still some narrowing, so you’ll need to go back for another check."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2159-04-24 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2159-04-24 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’ll call you with an appointment in the next two weeks. If it closes again, they might need to place a stent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2159-04-24 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2159-04-24 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get a full dialysis session this afternoon. After that, you can go back to your normal M-W-F schedule."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2159-04-24 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs after the procedure look stable. Hemoglobin is a bit low, but expected. Potassium is now 5.8—still okay since you’ll dialyze soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2159-04-24 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood sugar? I’m diabetic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2159-04-24 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your glucose was high at 362, but that’s common in the hospital. We kept your insulin lower since you were NPO. At home, go back to your usual dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2159-04-24 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I check it at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2159-04-24 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, check your blood sugar regularly. If it’s below 100, reduce your glargine to 7 units and call your doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2159-04-24 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2159-04-24 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go home on all your usual medications—amlodipine, aspirin, sevelamer, pravastatin, and the rest. We restarted your gabapentin today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2159-04-24 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2159-04-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re doing well. Your fistula has a strong thrill, and you’re stable. We’re clearing you to go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2159-04-25 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. When will I hear about the follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2159-04-25 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The radiology team will call you within the next two weeks to schedule the next procedure. Keep checking your fistula daily for a thrill."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2159-04-25 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And dialysis on Monday as usual?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2159-04-25 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, resume your normal dialysis schedule. And don’t forget to monitor your blood sugar and take all your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2159-04-25 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2159-04-25 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2159-04-23 16:15:00",
    "admission_end": "2159-04-25 16:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A man with end-stage renal disease on hemodialysis, type II diabetes, and heart failure was admitted due to a thrombosed right brachiobasilic fistula. He underwent a successful thrombectomy and balloon angioplasty to restore blood flow, with residual stenosis noted in the central vein. He received a dialysis session during admission and was stabilized on his home medications. The interventional radiology team expressed concern about recurrent stenosis and will schedule a follow-up procedure within two weeks. He was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to resume dialysis, monitor blood glucose, and watch for fistula function.",
    "problems": [
      "Thrombosed fistula",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Chronic systolic and diastolic heart failure",
      "Diabetes mellitus type II with neuropathy",
      "Hypertension",
      "Hyperlipidemia",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Anxiety",
      "Constipation",
      "Vitamin D deficiency",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea",
      "Aortocoronary bypass status",
      "Awaiting organ transplant",
      "Long-term use of aspirin",
      "Long-term use of insulin"
    ]
  }
}
